{"explanation":"Update MasterKey to write version-1 current encrypted records with the persistent AndroidKeyStore-generated wrapping key identified as "currentMasterKey". Current-record decryption resolves only that stored generated key, while records without the discriminator continue to derive and use the PBKDF2 key as the legacy decrypt argument. The AndroidKeyStore cipher provider remains responsible for encryption parameters through the coordinated EncryptedKey overload, avoiding caller-supplied GCM parameters.","review_assumptions":["AndroidKeyStore and android.security.keystore.KeyGenParameterSpec/KeyProperties are available for this module's supported Android API levels, as required by the coordinated Encryptor current-key lifecycle.","The coordinated EncryptedKey.decrypt(SecretKey legacyKey, SecretKey currentKey) implementation does not dereference the unused null argument and selects currentKey only for version-1 records.","The shared "currentMasterKey" alias intentionally identifies one persistent device-local wrapping key used by both MasterKey and Encryptor current writes; a missing alias during a current-record read is treated as an InvalidKeyException rather than creating a replacement key that cannot decrypt the record."],"no_change_required":false,"decision":"MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW","confidence":"high","edits":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/MasterKey.java","original_code":"import java.io.IOException;
